\i\lang1033 and}{\b\lang1033 ,}{\lang1033  }{\i\lang1033 ou}{\b\i\lang1033 th}{\i\lang1033 ouse}{\lang1033 , }{\i\lang1033 scra}{\b\i\lang1033 p-h}{\i\lang1033 eap}{\lang1033  (to borrow my own examples from Lesson One). In Quenya, initial }{\i\lang1033 
kh}{\lang1033 - first became }{\i\lang1033 ch}{\lang1033  as in German }{\i\lang1033 ach}{\lang1033 ; later it was weakened to a sound like English }{\b\lang1033 h}{\lang1033 -. Original initial }{\i\lang1033 ph}{\lang1033 - became Quenya }{\b\lang1033 f}
{\lang1033 -. }{\i\lang1033 Th}{\lang1033 - first came to be pronounced somewhat like English }{\i\lang1033 th}{\lang1033  (as in }{\i\lang1033 think}{\lang1033 ); later this sound merged with }{\b\lang1033 s}{\lang1033 -. Thus primitive forms like }{
